-- title:
--   Toric ab-torsion lies in toric a- plus b-torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. the image of $p$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(N_0,p,A)$: a morphism $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` with `barPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$ equal to `genPt p`, a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f$ to `base p`, a relative group law on $f$ over `baseRing p`, and bijections of $J_0(N_0)$ with the sections of $f$ over the generic point and of $J_0(N_0)$ over the residue field of $A$ with the sections over the residue point; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`, the conjunction asserting the abelian-scheme property bundle for $f$, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois equivariance of `pts`, additivity of `ptsSp`, compatibility of reduction of points modulo $\ell$ under the relevant inputs, and representability of each Hecke operator by an endomorphism of $f$ respecting the group law. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` over these data, and let $a,b$ be positive coprime naturals. Then, inside the group $J_0(N_0 p)$, the subgroup $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}(ab)$ — the subgroup generated by the range of the toric-point family of $\mathcal{O}$ at level $ab$ — is contained in the join $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}(a) \sqcup \mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}(b)$, that is, in the sum of the corresponding subgroups at levels $a$ and $b$.
--
--   This is the Chinese-remainder splitting of the toric torsion attached to the Néron object at $p$ of $J_0(N_0p)$: torsion of composite coprime order is generated by its $a$- and $b$-parts. It is one of the elementary steps used in the proof that prime-to-$p$ toric torsion lies in the toric monodromy part, via [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.toricPts_le_toricMonodromyPart_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts).
